Closing Statement

SRI explores a simple but fundamental idea:

Intelligence admissibility emerges deterministically from structure — without requiring training, inference, or prediction as the source of correctness.

AI may generate outputs.
Structure determines whether intelligence is admissible before generation begins.

It is released to encourage:

- independent validation
- real-world testing
- safe experimentation

SRI is offered as a minimal, verifiable reference implementation of that possibility.
